\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af4\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af9\langfe1033{\loch
The dock shelter has to be sealed against the box. Loading through a curtain-only door counts every minute twice on the stopwatch. After the doors are shut, re-opening is limited to 4 minutes each time (customs, seal check, forgotten pallet) and three re-opens per load per day shift; the fourth needs the supervisor's name on the form. The unit stays ON with fans on high the whole time, and a manual defrost, if you want one, must finish at least 40 minutes before the first pallet. Going over the window is not a catastrophe by itself: write it down, and watch Tag 1 closely for the next 2 hours.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af11\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf18\f6\fs26\b\dbch\af10{\loch
5. The excursion ladder}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af4\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af9\langfe1033{\loch
Tidewalk raises an alarm when a tag drifts. The alarm is a courtesy, not the procedure. The procedure is the ladder below, and what counts is how far the reading is above setpoint (warm side) and for how long. Minutes out of band accumulate over a rolling 24 hours; they do not reset because the temperature came back for ten minutes and everyone breathed out. If the sum reaches 3 hours 15 minutes in any rolling 24 hours, the load is Red, whatever the individual dips looked like.}
