\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af4\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af9\langfe1033{\loch
Cold side: any tag below +0.5 \u176\'b0C for 30 minutes on a chilled load goes straight to Orange. Frozen is not fussy about cold, but the tomatoes in the other half of a split box are.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af4\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af9\langfe1033{\loch
Three things that are forbidden at every level. You do not change the setpoint to "help" the load. You do not open the doors to have a look, because looking costs more than the information is worth. And you do not take a tag out of the box to "reset" it. All three have happened, the last time in January 2013 at Gdynia, when it hit \u8722\'3f23 \u176\'b0C overnight, the sockets on pad B froze solid and 14 boxes of fish went to Red before sunrise because the night man tried all three. He is retired now. He was a lovely man.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af4\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af9\langfe1033{\loch
Since 14 June nobody can say "no one told us". That one was nine hours. Do not make it ten.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af11\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af6\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf18\f6\fs26\b\dbch\af10{\loch
6. Paperwork, or: how to survive an audit}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af4\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af9\langfe1033{\loch
Every load gets a form KC-OPS-114 (Loading and Excursion Record), filled in Tidewalk on the dock tablet, or on paper if the tablets are dead and then keyed in by the end of that shift. It must show: the container number, the seal number (bolt seal, photographed), the three tag IDs with positions, the pre-cool start and end times, the stopwatch time of the loading window, and the three hand-probe readings. Minimum four photographs: the load pattern from the rear before closing, the top gap under the red line, the tags in place, and the seal.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af4\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af9\langfe1033{\loch
After an excursion of Level 2 or higher, the tag data is downloaded within 2 hours. For Level 3 and Level 4 an Excursion Report goes into Tidewalk, ticket category EXC, within 24 hours, and for Level 4 the full 8D root-cause report is due within 10 working days. Records are kept 7 years, or 12 years for GDP files. The loader and the supervisor both sign KC-OPS-114; the supervisor's signature means "I looked", not "I trust him". Quality audits roughly one form in twelve, and Benedikta can spot a form signed in advance from across the room.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af4\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\f4\fs22\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af9\langfe1033{\loch
Questions to me, not to the internet. The canteen is not a document control centre.}
